1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:03,155
Euclid's Elements, Book One, Proposition One.

2
00:00:03,155 --> 00:00:06,376
Construct an equilateral triangle on a given segment.

3
00:00:06,376 --> 00:00:10,570
Given segment A B, we are to construct an equilateral triangle on it.

4
00:00:10,990 --> 00:00:15,284
Construct circle A B, with center A and defining radius point B.

5
00:00:15,284 --> 00:00:19,914
Then construct circle B A, with center B and defining radius point A.

6
00:00:19,914 --> 00:00:24,880
From point C, where the circles intersect, construct segments C A and C B.

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,582
Since A is the center of circle A B, segment A C equals segment A B.

8
00:00:29,582 --> 00:00:33,864
Since B is the center of circle B A, segment B C equals segment B A.

9
00:00:33,864 --> 00:00:41,042
By Common Notion One, things equal to the same thing are equal to one another, so A C, A B, and B C are all equal.

10
00:00:41,042 --> 00:00:48,220
Therefore triangle A B C is equilateral, and has been constructed on the given segment A B, as was required to do.
